-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 21 (COSTS), Division 1 -- General: rules 1 to 9 and 11 to 16 (rule 10, fixed costs, is with Appendix 1
-- in roc5-o21-appendix.l4).  LAYER 1: the law, objectively.  Divisions 2 to 6 are in roc5-o21-assessment.l4,
-- which this module imports because rule 1(2) points to rule 22 for "indemnity basis" and "standard basis".
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT: as in roc5-o20.l4.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are the text's own yes and no;
-- NOTHING is "not covered"; a caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- "Subject to any written law" and "subject to this Order" are not threaded as inputs (NOTES.md): each
-- function answers its own provision.  "Unless the Court otherwise orders" IS an input where the rule says it.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 21, Division 1 -- General`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- definitions and general matters of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): this Order applies to the costs of or incidental to contentious business, and to any other proceedings
-- "if any written law provides or if the parties to any proceedings consent".  "Contentious business" has the
-- meaning given by section 2(1) of the Legal Profession Act (an input).
-- src:2909 | 1. —(1) This Order applies to the costs of or incidental to contentious business and to any other proceedings if any written law provides or if the parties to any proceedings consent. (2) In this Order — “assessed costs” means costs assessed in accordance with this Order;
@ref O 21 r 1(1) (src:2909-2909)
GIVEN `legal profession act s 2(1) the business is contentious business` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `any written law provides that this Order applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties consent that this Order applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 1(1) this Order applies to the costs` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `legal profession act s 2(1) the business is contentious business` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `any written law provides that this Order applies` OR `the parties consent that this Order applies`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `legal profession act s 2(1) the business is contentious business` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "contentious business" has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Legal Profession Act
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any other proceedings if any written law provides or if the parties to any proceedings consent"

-- (2): the definitions.
-- src:2909 | 1. —(1) This Order applies to the costs of or incidental to contentious business and to any other proceedings if any written law provides or if the parties to any proceedings consent. (2) In this Order — “assessed costs” means costs assessed in accordance with this Order;
@ref O 21 r 1(2) term assessed costs (src:2909-2909)
GIVEN `the costs were assessed in accordance with this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 1(2) costs are assessed costs` MEANS
    IF `the costs were assessed in accordance with this Order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“assessed costs” means costs assessed in accordance with this Order"

-- src:2910 | “contentious business” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Legal Profession Act;
@ref O 21 r 1(2) term contentious business (src:2910-2910)
GIVEN `legal profession act s 2(1) the business is contentious business` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 1(2) the business is contentious business` MEANS
    CONSIDER `legal profession act s 2(1) the business is contentious business`
    WHEN JUST answer THEN JUST answer -- the answer is section 2(1) of the Legal Profession Act's: "has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Legal Profession Act"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 2(1) of the Legal Profession Act is not among the sources

DECLARE `o 21 r 1(2) kind of charge` IS ONE OF
    `o 21 r 1(2) a fee`
    `o 21 r 1(2) a charge`
    `o 21 r 1(2) a disbursement`
    `o 21 r 1(2) an expense`
    `o 21 r 1(2) remuneration`
    `o 21 r 1(2) another kind of charge`

-- src:2911 | “costs” includes fees, charges, disbursements, expenses and remuneration;
@ref O 21 r 1(2) term costs (src:2911-2911)
GIVEN charge IS A `o 21 r 1(2) kind of charge`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 1(2) a charge is within costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER charge
    WHEN `o 21 r 1(2) another kind of charge` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“costs” includes fees, charges, disbursements, expenses and remuneration" and the list is not closed
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2912 | “indemnity basis” has the meaning given by Rule 22(3);
@ref O 21 r 1(2) term indemnity basis (src:2912-2912)
GIVEN basis IS A `o 21 r 22 basis of assessment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 1(2) the basis is the indemnity basis` MEANS
    `o 21 r 22(3) the basis is the indemnity basis` basis

-- src:2913 | “standard basis” has the meaning given by Rule 22(2).
@ref O 21 r 1(2) term standard basis (src:2913-2913)
GIVEN basis IS A `o 21 r 22 basis of assessment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 1(2) the basis is the standard basis` MEANS
    `o 21 r 22(2) the basis is the standard basis` basis

-- (3): references to a fund.
-- src:2914 | (3) In this Order — ( a )
-- src:2915 | references to a fund, being a fund out of which costs are to be paid or which is held by a trustee or personal representative, include references to any estate or property, whether movable or immovable, held for the benefit of any person or class of persons; and
@ref O 21 r 1(3)(a) (src:2914-2915)
GIVEN `it is a fund out of which costs are to be paid or which is held by a trustee or personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is an estate or property, whether movable or immovable, held for the benefit of any person or class of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 1(3)(a) a reference to a fund includes a reference to the thing` MEANS
    IF `it is a fund out of which costs are to be paid or which is held by a trustee or personal representative` AND `the thing is an estate or property, whether movable or immovable, held for the benefit of any person or class of persons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to a fund ... include references to any estate or property" and the list is not closed

-- src:2916 | ( b )
-- src:2917 | references to a fund held by a trustee or personal representative include references to any fund to which the trustee or personal representative is entitled (whether alone or together with any other person) in that capacity, whether the fund is for the time being in the possession of the trustee or personal representative or not.
@ref O 21 r 1(3)(b) (src:2916-2917)
GIVEN `it is a fund held by a trustee or personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a fund to which the trustee or personal representative is entitled in that capacity, alone or together with any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 1(3)(b) a reference to a fund held by a trustee or personal representative includes a reference to the thing` MEANS
    IF `it is a fund held by a trustee or personal representative` AND `the thing is a fund to which the trustee or personal representative is entitled in that capacity, alone or together with any other person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to a fund held by a trustee or personal representative include references to any fund to which the trustee or personal representative is entitled" and the list is not closed

