@ref O 21 r 2(2) (src:2919-2934)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `o 21 r 2(2) circumstance`
      `the Court is exercising its power to fix or assess costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstance is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 2(2) the Court must have regard to the circumstance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Court is exercising its power to fix or assess costs`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In exercising its power to fix or assess costs"
        IF circumstance EQUALS `o 21 r 2(2) another circumstance` AND (NOT `the circumstance is relevant`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "all relevant circumstances, including" and the text does not say what the Court does with a circumstance that is not relevant
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

