-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3 -- entitlement to costs`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1): "no party is entitled to recover any costs ... except under an order of the Court": a flat negative where
-- there is no order.  With an order, or under a later provision of this Order, the entitlement is what that order
-- or provision says.
-- src:2942 | 3. —(1) Subject to the following provisions of this Order, no party is entitled to recover any costs of or incidental to any proceedings from any other party to the proceedings except under an order of the Court. (2) The Court must, subject to this Order, order the costs of any proceedings in favour of a successful party, except when it appears to the Court that in the circumstances of the case some other order should be made as to the whole or any part of the costs.
@ref O 21 r 3(1) (src:2942-2942)
GIVEN `there is an order of the Court for the costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a later provision of this Order entitles the party to the costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 3(1) a party is entitled to recover costs from another party` MEANS
    IF `there is an order of the Court for the costs` OR `a later provision of this Order entitles the party to the costs`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what the order or the later provision gives is theirs; paragraph (1) says only who is not entitled
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no party is entitled to recover any costs of or incidental to any proceedings from any other party to the proceedings except under an order of the Court"

-- src:2942 | 3. —(1) Subject to the following provisions of this Order, no party is entitled to recover any costs of or incidental to any proceedings from any other party to the proceedings except under an order of the Court. (2) The Court must, subject to this Order, order the costs of any proceedings in favour of a successful party, except when it appears to the Court that in the circumstances of the case some other order should be made as to the whole or any part of the costs.
@ref O 21 r 3(2) (src:2942-2942)
GIVEN `the party is a successful party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Court that in the circumstances of the case some other order should be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 3(2) the Court must order the costs in favour of the successful party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the party is a successful party`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in favour of a successful party"
        IF `it appears to the Court that in the circumstances of the case some other order should be made`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except when it appears to the Court that in the circumstances of the case some other order should be made as to the whole or any part of the costs"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2943 | (3) The costs of and occasioned by any amendment made without permission in the originating claim or any pleadings must be borne by the party making the amendment, unless the Court otherwise orders.
@ref O 21 r 3(3) (src:2943-2943)
GIVEN `the amendment was made without permission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made in the originating claim or any pleadings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 3(3) the party making the amendment bears the costs of and occasioned by it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the amendment was made without permission` AND `it was made in the originating claim or any pleadings`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any amendment made without permission in the originating claim or any pleadings"
        IF `the Court has otherwise ordered`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Court otherwise orders"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2944 | (4) The costs of and occasioned by any application to extend the time fixed by these Rules or the Court, for serving or filing any document or doing any other act must be borne by the party making the application, unless the Court otherwise orders.
@ref O 21 r 3(4) (src:2944-2944)
GIVEN `it is an application to extend the time fixed by these Rules or the Court for serving or filing any document or doing any other act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 3(4) the party making the application bears the costs of and occasioned by it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is an application to extend the time fixed by these Rules or the Court for serving or filing any document or doing any other act`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any application to extend the time fixed by these Rules or the Court"
        IF `the Court has otherwise ordered`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Court otherwise orders"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `o 21 r 3(5) capacity` IS ONE OF
    `o 21 r 3(5) trustee`
    `o 21 r 3(5) personal representative`
    `o 21 r 3(5) mortgagee`
    `o 21 r 3(5) another capacity`

-- src:2945 | (5) Where a person is or has been a party to any proceedings in the capacity of trustee, personal representative or mortgagee, that person is, unless the Court otherwise orders, entitled to the costs of those proceedings, insofar as they are not recovered from or paid by any other person, out of the fund held by the trustee or personal representative or out of the mortgaged property, as the case may be.
@ref O 21 r 3(5) (src:2945-2945)
GIVEN capacity IS A `o 21 r 3(5) capacity`
      `the person is or has been a party to the proceedings in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 3(5) the person is entitled to the costs out of the fund or the mortgaged property` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF capacity EQUALS `o 21 r 3(5) another capacity` OR (NOT `the person is or has been a party to the proceedings in that capacity`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a person is or has been a party to any proceedings in the capacity of trustee, personal representative or mortgagee"
        IF `the Court has otherwise ordered`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Court otherwise orders"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "insofar as they are not recovered from or paid by any other person": the balance of the costs.
-- src:2945 | (5) Where a person is or has been a party to any proceedings in the capacity of trustee, personal representative or mortgagee, that person is, unless the Court otherwise orders, entitled to the costs of those proceedings, insofar as they are not recovered from or paid by any other person, out of the fund held by the trustee or personal representative or out of the mortgaged property, as the case may be.
@ref O 21 r 3(5) (src:2945-2945)
GIVEN `the costs of the proceedings` IS A NUMBER
      `the part recovered from or paid by any other person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 21 r 3(5) the costs not recovered from or paid by any other person` MEANS
    IF `the part recovered from or paid by any other person` AT LEAST `the costs of the proceedings`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the costs of the proceedings` MINUS `the part recovered from or paid by any other person`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rules 4 to 8 -- adverse costs orders; litigants in person; persons lacking capacity`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Rule 4: the successful party's costs may be disallowed or reduced, or the party ordered to pay costs, "if" (a),
-- (b), (c) or (d).  Limb (c) refers to Order 5 (another part): whether the party has discharged the duty is an
-- input, and the limb holds when it has NOT.
-- src:2947 | 4. The Court may disallow or reduce a successful party’s costs or order that party to pay costs, if — ( a )
-- src:2948 | that party has failed to establish any claim or issue which that party has raised in any proceedings, thereby unnecessarily increasing the amount of time taken, the costs or the complexity of the proceedings;
-- src:2949 | ( b )
-- src:2950 | that party has done or omitted to do anything unreasonably;
-- src:2951 | ( c )
-- src:2952 | that party has not discharged that party’s duty to consider amicable resolution of the dispute or to make an offer of amicable resolution in accordance with Order 5; or
-- src:2953 | ( d )
-- src:2954 | that party has failed to comply with any order of court, any relevant pre‑action protocol or any practice direction.
@ref O 21 r 4 (src:2947-2954)
GIVEN `the party failed to establish a claim or issue it raised, thereby unnecessarily increasing the time, the costs or the complexity of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party did or omitted to do anything unreasonably` IS A BOOLEAN
      `o 5 the party has discharged its duty to consider amicable resolution or to make an offer of amicable resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the party failed to comply with an order of court, a relevant pre-action protocol or a practice direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 4 the Court may disallow or reduce the successful party's costs or order the party to pay costs` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the party failed to establish a claim or issue it raised, thereby unnecessarily increasing the time, the costs or the complexity of the proceedings`
           OR `the party did or omitted to do anything unreasonably`
           OR `o 5 the party has discharged its duty to consider amicable resolution or to make an offer of amicable resolution` EQUALS JUST FALSE
           OR `the party failed to comply with an order of court, a relevant pre-action protocol or a practice direction`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 5 the party has discharged its duty to consider amicable resolution or to make an offer of amicable resolution` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the duty in Order 5 was discharged is Order 5's answer
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if — ( a ) ... ( b ) ... ( c ) ... or ( d )"

-- Rule 5: costs against a non-party.
-- src:2956 | 5. —(1) Where it is just to do so, the Court may order costs against a non‑party if the non‑party has — ( a )
-- src:2957 | assigned the non‑party’s right in the action to a party in return for a share of any money or property which that party may recover in the action;
-- src:2958 | ( b )
-- src:2959 | contributed or agreed to contribute to a party’s costs in return for a share of any money or property which that party may recover in the action; or
-- src:2960 | ( c )
-- src:2961 | contributed or agreed to contribute to a party’s costs and actively instigates or encourages that party to continue with the action.
