      `the non-party assigned its right in the action to a party in return for a share of any money or property which that party may recover in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the non-party contributed or agreed to contribute to a party's costs in return for a share of any money or property which that party may recover in the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the non-party contributed or agreed to contribute to a party's costs and actively instigates or encourages that party to continue with the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 5(1) the Court may order costs against the non-party` MEANS
    IF `it is just to do so`
       AND (   `the non-party assigned its right in the action to a party in return for a share of any money or property which that party may recover in the action`
            OR `the non-party contributed or agreed to contribute to a party's costs in return for a share of any money or property which that party may recover in the action`
            OR `the non-party contributed or agreed to contribute to a party's costs and actively instigates or encourages that party to continue with the action`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where it is just to do so, the Court may order costs against a non‑party if the non‑party has"

