`o 21 r 9 the hours that must pass after assessment` MEANS 48

-- (1): discontinuance or withdrawal, or an action deemed discontinued: the defendant is entitled to costs
-- incurred to the time of discontinuance, "unless the Court otherwise orders".
-- src:2984 | 9. —(1) Where — ( a )
-- src:2985 | a claimant by notice in writing and without permission either wholly discontinues the claimant’s action against any defendant or withdraws any particular claim made by the claimant in an action against any defendant; or
-- src:2986 | ( b )
-- src:2987 | an action is deemed discontinued,
-- src:2988 | the defendant is, unless the Court otherwise orders, entitled to the defendant’s costs of the action or claim incurred to the time of discontinuance, which may be assessed if not agreed between the parties, and the defendant may sign judgment for the defendant’s assessed costs after 48 hours after assessment.
@ref O 21 r 9(1) (src:2984-2988)
GIVEN `the claimant by notice in writing and without permission wholly discontinued the action against the defendant or withdrew a particular claim against the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is deemed discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 9(1) the defendant is entitled to the costs incurred to the time of discontinuance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the claimant by notice in writing and without permission wholly discontinued the action against the defendant or withdrew a particular claim against the defendant` OR `the action is deemed discontinued`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where — ( a ) a claimant by notice in writing and without permission either wholly discontinues the claimant’s action ... or ( b ) an action is deemed discontinued" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]
        IF `the Court has otherwise ordered`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Court otherwise orders"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "may sign judgment for the defendant's assessed costs after 48 hours after assessment".
-- src:2984 | 9. —(1) Where — ( a )
