§§ `Rules 11 to 16 -- the Registrar's powers to assess costs`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3003 | 11. —(1) The Registrar of the Supreme Court has power to assess — ( a )
-- src:3004 | any costs of or arising out of any cause or matter in the Supreme Court the assessment of which is directed by an order of the Court;
-- src:3005 | ( b )
-- src:3006 | any costs directed to be paid by an award made on a reference to arbitration under any written law or pursuant to an arbitration agreement; and
-- src:3007 | ( c )
-- src:3008 | any costs the assessment of which is allowed or directed by or under any written law.
@ref O 21 r 11(1) (src:3003-3008)
GIVEN `the costs are of or arise out of a cause or matter in the Supreme Court and their assessment is directed by an order of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs are directed to be paid by an award made on a reference to arbitration under a written law or pursuant to an arbitration agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assessment of the costs is allowed or directed by or under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 11(1) the Registrar of the Supreme Court has power to assess the costs` MEANS
    IF `the costs are of or arise out of a cause or matter in the Supreme Court and their assessment is directed by an order of the Court`
       OR `the costs are directed to be paid by an award made on a reference to arbitration under a written law or pursuant to an arbitration agreement`
       OR `the assessment of the costs is allowed or directed by or under a written law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "has power to assess — ( a ) ... ( b ) ... ( c )" and no word closes the list

-- src:3009 | (2) The Registrar of the State Courts has power to assess — ( a )
-- src:3010 | any costs of or arising out of any cause or matter in the State Courts the assessment of which is directed by an order of the Court; and
-- src:3011 | ( b )
-- src:3012 | any costs the assessment of which is allowed or directed by or under any written law.
@ref O 21 r 11(2) (src:3009-3012)
GIVEN `the costs are of or arise out of a cause or matter in the State Courts and their assessment is directed by an order of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assessment of the costs is allowed or directed by or under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 11(2) the Registrar of the State Courts has power to assess the costs` MEANS
    IF `the costs are of or arise out of a cause or matter in the State Courts and their assessment is directed by an order of the Court`
       OR `the assessment of the costs is allowed or directed by or under a written law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "has power to assess — ( a ) ... ( b )" and no word closes the list

DECLARE `o 21 r 12 supplementary power` IS ONE OF
    `o 21 r 12(a) take an account of any dealings in money made in connection with the payment of the costs being assessed`
    `o 21 r 12(b) require any party represented jointly with any other party in any proceedings before the Registrar to be separately represented`
    `o 21 r 12(c) examine any witness in those proceedings`
    `o 21 r 12(d) direct the production of any document which may be relevant in connection with those proceedings`

-- src:3014 | 12. The Registrar may in assessing costs — ( a )
-- src:3015 | take an account of any dealings in money made in connection with the payment of the costs being assessed, if the Court so directs;
-- src:3016 | ( b )
-- src:3017 | require any party represented jointly with any other party in any proceedings before the Registrar to be separately represented;
-- src:3018 | ( c )
-- src:3019 | examine any witness in those proceedings; and
-- src:3020 | ( d )
-- src:3021 | direct the production of any document which may be relevant in connection with those proceedings.
@ref O 21 r 12 (src:3014-3021)
GIVEN power IS A `o 21 r 12 supplementary power`
      `the Court so directs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 12 the Registrar may do the thing in assessing costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER power
    WHEN `o 21 r 12(a) take an account of any dealings in money made in connection with the payment of the costs being assessed` THEN
        IF `the Court so directs`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Court so directs"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Rule 13.
-- src:3023 | 13. —(1) Subject to the provisions of any written law, the party whose bill is being assessed is entitled to the party’s costs of the assessment proceedings. (2) The party liable to pay the costs of the proceedings which gave rise to the assessment proceedings may make a written offer to pay a specific sum in satisfaction of those costs which is expressed to be “without prejudice except as to the costs of the assessment of costs”, at any time before the expiration of 14 days after the delivery to the party of a copy of the bill of costs under Rule 19 and, where such an offer is made, the fact that it has been made must not be communicated to the Registrar until the question of the costs of the assessment proceedings falls to be decided.
@ref O 21 r 13(1) (src:3023-3023)
GIVEN `the party's bill is being assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 13(1) the party is entitled to the costs of the assessment proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the party's bill is being assessed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the party whose bill is being assessed"

`o 21 r 13(2) the period for the offer` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- (2): the party liable to pay the costs of the proceedings which gave rise to the assessment may make a written
-- offer to pay a specific sum, expressed to be "without prejudice except as to the costs of the assessment of
-- costs", "at any time before the expiration of 14 days after the delivery to the party of a copy of the bill of
-- costs under Rule 19".
-- src:3023 | 13. —(1) Subject to the provisions of any written law, the party whose bill is being assessed is entitled to the party’s costs of the assessment proceedings. (2) The party liable to pay the costs of the proceedings which gave rise to the assessment proceedings may make a written offer to pay a specific sum in satisfaction of those costs which is expressed to be “without prejudice except as to the costs of the assessment of costs”, at any time before the expiration of 14 days after the delivery to the party of a copy of the bill of costs under Rule 19 and, where such an offer is made, the fact that it has been made must not be communicated to the Registrar until the question of the costs of the assessment proceedings falls to be decided.
@ref O 21 r 13(2) (src:3023-3023)
GIVEN `the offer is a written offer to pay a specific sum in satisfaction of the costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer is expressed to be without prejudice except as to the costs of the assessment of costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the offer is made` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 13(2) the party liable may make the offer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the offer is a written offer to pay a specific sum in satisfaction of the costs` AND `the offer is expressed to be without prejudice except as to the costs of the assessment of costs`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "make a written offer to pay a specific sum in satisfaction of those costs which is expressed to be “without prejudice except as to the costs of the assessment of costs”"
        IF `the date the offer is made` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time before the expiration of 14 days after the delivery to the party of a copy of the bill of costs under Rule 19" [period, ruled 2026-11-05 (a)]

-- "the fact that it has been made must not be communicated to the Registrar until the question of the costs of
-- the assessment proceedings falls to be decided": an "until" bar (ruling of 2026-11-05 (d)).  The bar is
-- encoded as its own yes/no: JUST TRUE before the question falls to be decided, JUST FALSE after.  The
-- function never says that the fact has been, or may be, communicated.
-- src:3023 | 13. —(1) Subject to the provisions of any written law, the party whose bill is being assessed is entitled to the party’s costs of the assessment proceedings. (2) The party liable to pay the costs of the proceedings which gave rise to the assessment proceedings may make a written offer to pay a specific sum in satisfaction of those costs which is expressed to be “without prejudice except as to the costs of the assessment of costs”, at any time before the expiration of 14 days after the delivery to the party of a copy of the bill of costs under Rule 19 and, where such an offer is made, the fact that it has been made must not be communicated to the Registrar until the question of the costs of the assessment proceedings falls to be decided.
@ref O 21 r 13(2) (src:3023-3023)
GIVEN `the question of the costs of the assessment proceedings has fallen to be decided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 13(2) the fact of the offer cannot yet be communicated to the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the question of the costs of the assessment proceedings has fallen to be decided`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be communicated to the Registrar until the question of the costs of the assessment proceedings falls to be decided" [until bar: delegated-definitions ruling (d) of 2026-11-05]
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:3024 | (3) The Registrar may take into account any offer made under paragraph (2) which has been brought to the Registrar’s attention.
@ref O 21 r 13(3) (src:3024-3024)
GIVEN `the offer was made under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer has been brought to the Registrar's attention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 13(3) the Registrar may take the offer into account` MEANS
    IF `the offer was made under paragraph (2)` AND `the offer has been brought to the Registrar's attention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any offer made under paragraph (2) which has been brought to the Registrar’s attention"

-- Rule 14.
-- src:3026 | 14. —(1) The Registrar may, from time to time in the course of the assessment of any costs by the Registrar, issue an interim certificate for any part of those costs which has been assessed. (2) If, in the course of the assessment of a solicitor’s bill to the solicitor’s own client, it appears to the Registrar that in any event the solicitor will be liable in connection with that bill to pay money to the client, the Registrar may from time to time issue an interim certificate specifying an amount which in the Registrar’s opinion is payable by the solicitor to the client.
@ref O 21 r 14(1) (src:3026-3026)
GIVEN `the Registrar is in the course of assessing costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `part of the costs has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 14(1) the Registrar may issue an interim certificate for the part assessed` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is in the course of assessing costs` AND `part of the costs has been assessed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the course of the assessment of any costs by the Registrar, issue an interim certificate for any part of those costs which has been assessed"

-- src:3026 | 14. —(1) The Registrar may, from time to time in the course of the assessment of any costs by the Registrar, issue an interim certificate for any part of those costs which has been assessed. (2) If, in the course of the assessment of a solicitor’s bill to the solicitor’s own client, it appears to the Registrar that in any event the solicitor will be liable in connection with that bill to pay money to the client, the Registrar may from time to time issue an interim certificate specifying an amount which in the Registrar’s opinion is payable by the solicitor to the client.
@ref O 21 r 14(2) (src:3026-3026)
GIVEN `it is the assessment of a solicitor's bill to the solicitor's own client` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Registrar that in any event the solicitor will be liable in connection with that bill to pay money to the client` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 14(2) the Registrar may issue an interim certificate specifying an amount payable by the solicitor to the client` MEANS
    IF `it is the assessment of a solicitor's bill to the solicitor's own client` AND `it appears to the Registrar that in any event the solicitor will be liable in connection with that bill to pay money to the client`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, in the course of the assessment of a solicitor’s bill to the solicitor’s own client, it appears to the Registrar that in any event the solicitor will be liable"

-- src:3027 | (3) On the filing of a certificate issued under paragraph (2), the Court may order the amount specified in the certificate to be paid forthwith to the client or into Court.
@ref O 21 r 14(3) (src:3027-3027)
GIVEN `a certificate issued under paragraph (2) has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 14(3) the Court may order the amount to be paid forthwith to the client or into Court` MEANS
    IF `a certificate issued under paragraph (2) has been filed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the filing of a certificate issued under paragraph (2)" [on counts as where: delegated-definitions ruling (c) of 2026-11-05]

-- Rule 15.
-- src:3029 | 15. Where a party entitled to be paid costs is also liable to pay costs, the Registrar may — ( a )
-- src:3030 | assess the costs which that party is liable to pay and set off the amount allowed against the amount that party is entitled to be paid and direct payment of any balance; or
-- src:3031 | ( b )
-- src:3032 | delay the issue of a certificate for the costs that party is entitled to be paid until that party has paid or tendered the amount that party is liable to pay.
@ref O 21 r 15 (src:3029-3032)
GIVEN `a party entitled to be paid costs is also liable to pay costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 15 the Registrar may assess the costs the party is liable to pay and set them off, or delay the certificate` MEANS
    IF `a party entitled to be paid costs is also liable to pay costs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a party entitled to be paid costs is also liable to pay costs, the Registrar may" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]

-- Rule 16.
-- src:3034 | 16. —(1) Where the Court directs an account to be taken and the account consists in part of a bill of costs, the Court may direct the Registrar to assess those costs, and the Registrar must do so and return the bill of costs, after assessment of the bill of costs, together with the Registrar’s report on the bill of costs to the Court. (2) The Registrar assessing a bill of costs in accordance with a direction under this Rule has the same powers, and the same fees are payable in connection with the assessment, as if an order for assessment of the costs had been made by the Court.
@ref O 21 r 16(1) (src:3034-3034)
GIVEN `the Court directs an account to be taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the account consists in part of a bill of costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 21 r 16(1) the Court may direct the Registrar to assess the costs, and the Registrar must do so` MEANS
    IF `the Court directs an account to be taken` AND `the account consists in part of a bill of costs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Court directs an account to be taken and the account consists in part of a bill of costs" [where, ruled 2026-11-05 (b)]

-- src:3034 | 16. —(1) Where the Court directs an account to be taken and the account consists in part of a bill of costs, the Court may direct the Registrar to assess those costs, and the Registrar must do so and return the bill of costs, after assessment of the bill of costs, together with the Registrar’s report on the bill of costs to the Court. (2) The Registrar assessing a bill of costs in accordance with a direction under this Rule has the same powers, and the same fees are payable in connection with the assessment, as if an order for assessment of the costs had been made by the Court.
@ref O 21 r 16(2) (src:3034-3034)
